# The re-adjudicated arms of roadmap 2.9 are whole-movement Logs (hundreds of
# MB each) and are REPRODUCIBLE from the shared record by run_scan.sh. The
# small artefacts beside them -- the MusicXML, the coverage census, the
# simulate rows and the run logs -- are what the FINDINGS cite, and they stay.
*-base.json
*-arm.json

# The whole-movement MusicXML is 3-6 MB per arm and is REPRODUCIBLE by
# run_scan_lean.py from the shared record. What the FINDINGS cite is beside
# it and IS committed: the coverage census, the lean report, and the
# per-part fifths table (*.fifths.txt) that every key figure is read off.
litolff-base.musicxml
litolff-arm.musicxml
brahms-base.musicxml
brahms-arm.musicxml

# Roadmap 2.9b's arms, same rule and same reason: the whole-movement MusicXML
# is 1.8-3 MB per arm and reproducible from the shared record by
# `readjudicate.py` + `staged.export`. What the FINDINGS cite is committed
# beside it -- `*.part-report.txt`, the per-staff table every 2.9b figure is
# read off.
2.9b-litolff-base.musicxml
2.9b-litolff-arm.musicxml
2.9b-breitkopf-base.musicxml
2.9b-breitkopf-arm.musicxml
